# Node implementation

- Implement `INodeType`. Prefer declarative routing (`requestDefaults`) when the node is HTTP mapping; use `execute` for custom logic.
- Version with `version: [1, 1.1]` or a `VersionedNodeType` class. Follow the existing node's versioning style.
- Throw `NodeOperationError` for user-facing failures and `NodeApiError` for upstream API failures. Honor `continueOnFail` when the node already does.
- No `any`. Prefer type guards over `as` outside tests.
- Values from `this.getNodeParameter(...)` and `item.json` are untrusted. Do not use them as computed keys on assignment. Write through `setSafeObjectProperty` / `isSafeObjectProperty` from `n8n-workflow`, or use a `Map` / `Object.create(null)`.

```ts
import { isSafeObjectProperty, setSafeObjectProperty } from 'n8n-workflow';

if (isSafeObjectProperty(table) && acc[table] === undefined) {
  setSafeObjectProperty(acc, table, {});
}
```

- Tests live next to the node. Mock HTTP with `nock`. Run `pnpm test <file>` from `packages/nodes-base`.
- Read `packages/nodes-base/AGENTS.md` before adding a node, trigger, or credential.
